## Description

XML documentation on `[AsParameters]` properties is dropped when the binding attribute is declared on a positional record's primary constructor parameter.

The operation transformer emitted by the XML comment source generator resolves the OpenAPI parameter for a property-bound `ApiParameterDescription` from attributes it finds by reflecting over the *property*:

```csharp
var modelName = GetModelName(propertyInfo, propertyInfo.Name);
var parameter = GetOperationParameter(operation, modelName);
```

For a positional record the attribute lives on the constructor parameter, not on the generated property, so `GetModelName` falls back to the property name (`Version`) while the OpenAPI parameter is named after the binder (`x-client-version`). The lookup misses and the documentation is silently discarded.

```csharp
/// <param name="Version">The version of the client application.</param>
/// <param name="DeviceId">The identifier of the client device.</param>
public record ClientInfo(
    [FromHeader(Name = "x-client-version")] string Version,
    [FromHeader(Name = "x-client-device-id")] string? DeviceId);

app.MapPost("/login", ([AsParameters] ClientInfo clientInfo, LoginRequest request) => TypedResults.Ok());
```

Before this change both header parameters are emitted without a `description`. `ApiParameterDescription.Name` already carries the name the binder resolved, for attributes declared on the property *or* on the constructor parameter, so the lookup now prefers it and keeps the reflection-derived name as a fallback.

This is the same family of problem as #69436. The form reported there — the attribute declared directly on the property — is already handled on `main` by the `GetModelName` / request-body-source changes; the constructor-parameter form is not, and on 10.x both forms also leak the property documentation into `requestBody.description`.

## Changes

* `XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs`: resolve the operation parameter from `parameterDescription.Name`, falling back to the existing reflection-based model name.
* Regression test in `OperationTests.MinimalApis.cs` covering header-bound properties on a positional record, asserting the descriptions land on the parameters and do not leak into the request body.
* Existing generator snapshots updated for the emitted code change.

